At the front, the Revuelto includes a set of brand new Y-shaped day-time running [[Light-emitting diode|LED]] lights with the main headlights located at the top corners of the running lights.<ref name="auto4">{{Cite web|url=https://www.motor1.com/news/659544/lamborghini-revuelto-debuts-aerospace-inspired-v12-hybrid/|title=2024 Lamborghini Revuelto Debuts: Aerospace-Inspired V12 Hybrid With 1,001 HP|date=March 29, 2023|website=Motor1.com}}</ref> The car also features Lamborghini's ALA (Aerodinamica Lamborghini Attiva) system, which is said to be 80% lighter than regular sports car hydraulic systems having redesigned vents underneath the headlights and behind the [[scissor doors]].

At the rear, the Revuelto features an active aero [[Spoiler (car)|spoiler]] which produces more downforce than its predecessor. The tail-lights feature the same Y-shaped design as the headlights.

The Revuelto has its exhaust tips positioned between the taillights, with the rear spoiler being shaped around them. Another feature setting the Revuelto apart from its predecessors is the completely exposed engine bay, similar to the [[Bugatti Veyron]] and [[Bugatti Chiron|Chiron]].

===Interior===
The Revuelto features increased interior space, improving comfort for its occupants. It also has a new hybrid driving mode called "Città," Italian for "city."<ref name="auto3"/> This driving mode reduces the power-output of the car for daily usage and extra comfort while driving on urban roads. The car's redesigned instrument cluster shows the state of charge and energy recovery. It also displays the music being played by the [[In-car entertainment|infotainment system]] and fuel usage which separates on the left and right sides of the main display. The 8.4 inch vertical centre display supports [[Amazon Alexa]], [[CarPlay|Apple CarPlay]] and [[Android Auto]]. The car features a small display located in front of the passenger that monitors the speed, selected gear and the car's state.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Rehbock |first=Billy |title=2024 Lamborghini Revuelto Review: Expert Insights, Pricing, and Trims |url=https://www.motortrend.com/cars/lamborghini/revuelto/ |access-date=2025-06-09 |website=MotorTrend |language=en}}</ref>

==Specifications==
===Body===
The Revuelto has a [[monocoque]] composed entirely of carbon fibre, making it 10% lighter than the Aventador's chassis.<ref name="auto">{{Cite web|url=https://www.autoevolution.com/news/official-lamborghini-revuelto-retires-aventador-packs-1001-hp-hybrid-v12-217-mph-chops-212613.html|title=Official: Lamborghini Revuelto Retires Aventador, Packs 1,001-HP Hybrid V12, 217 MPH Chops|first=Florin|last=Amariei|date=March 29, 2023|website=autoevolution}}</ref> [[Torsional rigidity]] has been improved by 25% and the front frame is 20% lighter.<ref name="auto"/><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.autoexpress.co.uk/lamborghini/revuelto|title=New Lamborghini Revuelto: plug-in hybrid V12 supercar revealed|date=March 29, 2023|website=Auto Express}}</ref> Lamborghini has used carbon fibre in the construction, and the back of the chassis contains high-strength aluminium alloys.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.autoplus.fr/lamborghini/lamborghini-revuelto-information-photo-877478.html|title=Lamborghini Revuelto : la nouvelle supercar hybride V12 de 1 015 ch|date=March 29, 2023|website=Auto Plus}}</ref>

===Powertrain===
The Revuelto features a new [[Lamborghini V12|6.5-liter]] [[V12 engine]], complemented by three electric motors that produce a combined power of {{cvt|746.5|kW|PS|0}}.<ref>{{Cite web | url= https://motorlane.in/car-news/lamborghini-revuelto-launched-in-india | title= Powerful Lamborghini Revuelto Launched in India: Unveiling the Hybrid Supercar at Rs 8.89 Crore | publisher= Motorlane | date= December 11, 2023 | access-date= February 8, 2024 | archive-date= March 15, 2024 | archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20240315201236/https://motorlane.in/car-news/lamborghini-revuelto-launched-in-india/ | url-status= dead }}</ref><ref name="auto4"/>
