== Models ==
=== Revuelto SV (2026) ===
On 14 August 2026, Lamborghini unveiled the new Revuelto SV.<ref>{{cite web |title=Lamborghini Revuelto SV: The Quantum of Driving |url=https://www.lamborghini.com/en-en/news/Lamborghini-Revuelto-SV-The-Quantum-of-Driving |website=lamborghini.com |publisher=lamborghini.com |access-date=14 August 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Extreme new Lamborghini Revuelto SV storms in with 1051bhp |url=https://www.autocar.co.uk/car-news/new-cars/extreme-new-lamborghini-revuelto-sv-storms-1051bhp |access-date=16 August 2026 |agency=autocar.co.uk/ |publisher=autocar.co.uk |date=14 August 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Lamborghini Revuelto SV revealed – 1050bhp supercar to face Aston Martin's Valhalla |url=https://www.evo.co.uk/lamborghini/revuelto/208668/lamborghini-revuelto-sv-revealed-1050bhp-supercar-to-face-aston-martins |access-date=16 August 2026 |agency=evo.co.uk |publisher=evo.co.uk |date=14 August 2026}}</ref>

==Variants==
===Opera Unica (2024)===
Through their Ad Personam division, Lamborghini has built a handful of one-off "Opera Unica" models based on standard Revueltos, and featuring unique, hand-painted liveries and custom interior details.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2024-11-11 |title=This one-off Lamborghini Revuelto is inspired by one of the brightest stars in the night sky |url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/first-look/one-lamborghini-revuelto-inspired-one-brightest-stars-night-sky |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241210114541/https://www.topgear.com/car-news/first-look/one-lamborghini-revuelto-inspired-one-brightest-stars-night-sky |archive-date=2024-12-10 |access-date=2025-08-31 |work=Top Gear |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Abidin |first=Shafiq |date=4 August 2024 |title=This is a one-off Lamborghini Revuelto inspired by the island of Sardinia |url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/first-look/a-one-lamborghini-revuelto-inspired-island-sardinia |website=Top Gear}}</ref>
